## Conclusion

The state of the art is not a single OKF product. It is a converging workflow:
portable Markdown, deterministic agent interfaces, separate conformance and
curation, git-native diffs, evidence-aware review, rebuildable indexes,
authenticated retrieval, MCP projection, and versioned evaluation.

Rocci already implements much of the difficult portable core and a useful
local review slice. The highest-leverage move is to make that core truly
embeddable and let rocs-okf become the focused first-party application. If the
source remains plain OKF, the engine remains UI-neutral, and every review and
query is revision- and evidence-aware, the system can become substantially
more capable without becoming a new silo.
